findings.span:
Boundary values and material properties used in the simu-lations were drawn from the same test-day measurements that governed the bench runs, with 95% confidence intervals carried through in 300-member ensembles per representative condition;
variation in hematocrit (38.5 ± 1.2%) and viscosity at 100 s1
(3.8 ± 0.2 mPa·s) were explicitly sampled, and input uncertainty accounted for 12–18% of the spread in predicted hemolysis across the three models.

